# An allowlist: the build context is what the repository versions, nothing else of the folder (a
# .env.local, .local/, a key, a venv). Only the `test` stage copies the whole context (docs/ included:
# tests/test_readme.py checks the links, paths and numbers in it); every other stage copies only what
# it runs. A new top-level file or folder of the repository goes here too.
*
!.dockerignore
!.gitignore
!Dockerfile
!LICENSE
!README.md
!api
!catalogo.py
!cli.py
!constraints.txt
!data
!docker-compose.yml
!docs
!exemplos
!generated
!guardrails
!mcp_servers
!pyproject.toml
!requirements.txt
!requirements-dev.txt
!runtime
!samples
!specs
!tests
!transpiler

# Inside those folders too, what .gitignore keeps out of the repository, and other local secrets and
# caches (tests/test_endurecimento.py checks every .gitignore pattern is here).
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*credentials*.json
**/secrets
**/.local
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.log
**/docker-compose.override.yml
generated/*
# The example env file (no secret: every value empty), read by tests/test_variaveis.py.
!.env.example
